          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em formal scheme
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+neighbourhood"} formal neighbourhood
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
          %p
            Generally this may be formalized via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-objects"} ind-objects
            of schemes. Hence regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
            of ordinary schemes (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Strickland00"} Strickland 00, section 4
          %p
            Regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+space"} locally ringed space
            a formal scheme has the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            of an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            contains extra nilpotent elements.
          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %p
            Formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[\![x_1,\ldots,x_n]\!]
            are limits of their truncations (e.g. in one variable
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[\![x]\!]/(x^n)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adic+topology"} adic topology
          %p
